title: Start
---

NPC: I believe that X because Y.
-> That's dumb.
    <<jump badArgument>>
-> You're dumb.
    <<jump badArgument>>
// this interrupts the yarn dialogue to give the player free input.
// from there, the input is evaluated
-> (free input)
    <<jump evaluate>>

===

title: badArgument
---

NPC: You haven't changed my mind.
<<jump Start>>

===

title: evaluate
---

NPC: hm
<<if $argumentIsValid and $foundConcept==$key>>
    NPC: dang i guess that makes sense
        <<jump end>>
<<elseif $argumentIsValid and $foundConcept != $key>>
    NPC: that's not what i'm talking about
    <<jump wrongConcept>>
<<elseif $foundConcept==$key>>
    NPC: okay that's true but your argument is invalid
    <<jump badArgument>>
<<else>>
    <<jump badArgument>>
<<endif>>

===
title: wrongConcept
---
<<if $foundConcept == "faith">>
    NPC: this is about science. science doesn't need faith.
    // these jump to wherever
    -> a
    -> b
    -> (free input)
        <<jump evaluate>>
<<elseif $foundConcept == "art">>
    NPC: this is about science. and i don't see how they relate.
    // these jump to wherever
    -> a
    -> b
    -> (free input)
        <<jump evaluate>>
<<else>>
    NPC: I don't see how that's related.
    -> You're right, it's not.
        <<jump badArgument>>
    -> (free input)
        <<jump evaluate>>
<<endif>>

===
title: end
---
NPC: ok bye
